tpm_buf_destroy(&buf);
return name_size_alg;
</text>
Reason:
The fix adds `tpm_buf_destroy(&buf)` before the return in both the error and success paths, ensuring the allocated `tpm_buf` is freed in all cases. This prevents the memory leak while preserving the original logic.

